{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Change the law to require websites to honour universal privacy preferences",
        "additional_details": "People can refuse non-essential advertising cookies, but repeatedly making the same decision on every website puts the burden on users. A legally recognised universal opt-out, set once on a browser or device, would make that choice automatic and reduce intrusive pop-ups. Websites could still ask for specific permissions, but ignoring or refusing a request must not count as consent. This petition asks Parliament to change the law, not merely issue guidance to individual website operators.",
        "background": "Amend UK privacy law so websites and apps must honour a standard browser or device-wide choice to refuse non-essential advertising and profiling trackers. The choice should apply automatically across services, without repeated consent banners. Essential functions would remain permitted.",
